---
// Timeoff — Cosign project page. SCAFFOLD.
// Same split as /work (left 3fr text / right 5fr media). Right column = stacked
// landscape demo placeholders, each footnoted; left = matching numbered text
// blocks, paired per grid row so each section aligns with its demo.
// Media are placeholders. Copy = RJ's voice, condensed.
const meta = 'Product Design · Front End · 2026';

// 4 beats = 4 demos. Beat 0 folds in the intro; each beat's paras render in order.
const beats = [
  [
    "Cosign came out of an interview process — I thought this'd be a breeze, but boy was I wrong. The brief was a patient chart portal for a family clinic… and that's about the only simple thing about it. Two views and access levels, timed access that expires, a notes lifecycle, and an audit view only the physician can see. Came together in roughly 5 days.",
    "I'd never designed anything like this, and it had to function just as good as it looked. I wasted a full day designing a chart from scratch — nothing worked, just ugly charts out of a 1980's textbook. So I went a different route and built it brick by brick: make the small parts look pretty and work well, then slot them together. I leaned on a weird mix of references — Google's styling and an art auction house's type — and landed on this type-forward, bento style grid that just worked. If I was a physician, this is the chart I'd want.",
  ],
  [
    "A quick demo of how I pulled off the “two view / two levels of access” thing. I leaned hard on these row “footers” — they didn't technically change the chart, but they carried the context and functionality I needed.",
  ],
  [
    "Now some of the fun stuff… the restricted access. The PA can see there's a restricted result — maybe he'd want to request it to give proper care — while the confidential note stays physician-only. Easy enough conceptually… whatever. But once that first layer is built and you run through it, you notice a new issue every time. Small stuff mostly, but that's what drives you nuts.",
  ],
  [
    "Now the notes and audit duo… thankfully the last things I built, so they slotted into an almost fully designed system. I gave them both a home in the bottom corners. Notes get a few handoffs and a lifecycle, plus a physician-only confidential note — and the audit tab is… well… just an audit tab with a few more features. Even at 90% done I spent more time on the last 10% than the first 90%… story of my life.",
  ],
];
const demoSrcs = ['/cosign-main.mp4', '/cosign-two-view.mp4', '/cosign-access.mp4', '/cosign-notes.mp4'];
const liveUrl = 'https://cosign-two.vercel.app';
const pad = (n) => String(n + 1).padStart(2, '0');
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Cosign — Timeoff</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Host+Grotesk:ital,wght@0,400..800;1,400..800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
    <style>
      :root {
        --ground: #ffffff;
        --ink: #101113;
        --ink-soft: #6f6f68;
        --ink-faint: #a5a49c;
        --placeholder: #ECEBE7;
        --font: "Host Grotesk", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--ground);
        color: var(--ink);
        font-family: var(--font);
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
        text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
      }

      /* persistent brand — top center, tucks up on scroll (same as /work) */
      .brand {
        position: fixed;
        top: 1.1rem;
        left: 50%;
        transform: translateX(-50%) translateY(0);
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        font-weight: 500;
        letter-spacing: 0.01em;
        color: var(--ink);
        text-decoration: none;
        z-index: 3;
        transition: transform 0.26s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1), opacity 0.22s ease;
      }
      .brand.tucked {
        transform: translateX(-50%) translateY(-160%);
        opacity: 0;
        pointer-events: none;
      }
      .back {
        position: fixed;
        top: 1.1rem;
        left: 1.25rem;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        font-weight: 500;
        color: var(--ink);
        text-decoration: none;
        z-index: 3;
      }
      .back { transition: opacity 0.2s ease; }
      .back:hover { opacity: 0.55; }

      /* same split + spacing as the /work grid; each text block pairs with its
         demo on the same row and aligns at the top */
      .beats {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 3fr 5fr;
        column-gap: 2.75rem;
        row-gap: 6rem;
        align-items: start;
        padding: 5.5rem 1.5rem 6rem;
        max-width: 1600px;
        margin: 0 auto;
      }

      .fn {
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        font-weight: 500;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        color: var(--ink-faint);
        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
        margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
      }

      .beat-text { max-width: 36ch; }
      .proj-title { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 0.35rem; }
      .title-row { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.55rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 0 0 0.35rem; }
      .title-row .proj-title { margin: 0; }
      .live-link { font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink-faint); text-decoration: none; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.2rem; transition: color 0.15s ease; }
      .live-link:hover { color: var(--ink); }
      .live-link svg { width: 0.72em; height: 0.72em; }
      .proj-meta { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 1.4rem; }
      .beat-text p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.98rem; line-height: 1.6; }
      .beat-text p + p { margin-top: 1.1rem; }

      .media { aspect-ratio: 1672 / 1080; background: var(--placeholder); border-radius: 2px; width: 100%; overflow: hidden; }
      .media video { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }

      /* entrance: fade + rise, slight per-beat stagger */
      .beat-text, .beat-media {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateY(14px);
        animation: rise 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1) forwards;
        animation-delay: calc(var(--i) * 90ms);
      }
      @keyframes rise { to { opacity: 1; transform: none; } }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .beat-text, .beat-media { opacity: 1; transform: none; animation: none; }
        .brand { transition: opacity 0.3s ease; }
        .brand.tucked { transform: translateX(-50%) translateY(0); }
      }

      @media (max-width: 900px) {
        .beats { grid-template-columns: 1fr; row-gap: 2.5rem; }
        .beat-text { max-width: none; }
        .beat-media .fn { display: none; }
      }
      @media (max-width: 768px) {
        .beats { padding: 5rem 1.2rem 4rem; column-gap: 1.4rem; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="back" href="/work">Work</a>
    <a class="brand" href="/">timeoff</a>

    <main class="beats">
      {beats.map((paras, i) => (
        <>
          <div class="beat-text" style={`--i:${i}`}>
            <div class="fn">{pad(i)}</div>
            {i === 0 && (
              <div class="title-row">
                <h1 class="proj-title">Cosign</h1>
                <a class="live-link" href={liveUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Live<svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 9L9 3M9 3H4M9 3V8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
              </div>
            )}
            {i === 0 && <p class="proj-meta">{meta}</p>}
            {paras.map((para) => <p>{para}</p>)}
          </div>
          <div class="beat-media" style={`--i:${i}`}>
            <div class="fn">{pad(i)}</div>
            <div class="media">
              <video class="demo" src={demoSrcs[i]} poster={demoSrcs[i].replace(/\.(mp4|mov)$/, '.jpg')} muted loop playsinline preload="none"></video>
            </div>
          </div>
        </>
      ))}
    </main>

    <script is:inline>
      // brand tucks up + fades once scrolled off the top; returns at the top
      (function () {
        var brand = document.querySelector('.brand');
        if (!brand) return;
        var THRESHOLD = 6, ticking = false;
        function update() { brand.classList.toggle('tucked', window.scrollY > THRESHOLD); ticking = false; }
        window.addEventListener('scroll', function () {
          if (!ticking) { window.requestAnimationFrame(update); ticking = true; }
        }, { passive: true });
        update();
      })();

      // demo videos play only while in view (muted, looping)
      (function () {
        var vids = document.querySelectorAll('video.demo');
        if (!vids.length || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) return;
        var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
          entries.forEach(function (en) {
            if (en.isIntersecting) { var p = en.target.play(); if (p && p.catch) p.catch(function () {}); }
            else { en.target.pause(); }
          });
        }, { threshold: 0.4 });
        vids.forEach(function (v) { io.observe(v); });
      })();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
